message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal example of an “interactive rotating card” that flips when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste this into an `.html` file (or add the CSS to your stylesheet) and tweak the colors, size, or content as you like.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    background:#f0f2f5;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    margin:0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card itself ---------- */
.card {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform .6s ease-in-out;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* Hover triggers rotation */
.card:hover { 
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* Rotate around Y axis (horizontal flip) */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front & Back faces ---------- */
.front,
.back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* Hide the reverse side while turned */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.25);
}

.front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* Start rotated so it's hidden initially */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Sample content styling ---------- */
h2{
    margin:0 0 10px;
}
p{
    margin:0;
}
```

