<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front face -->
        <div class="front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/250/150?random=1" alt="Random image" style="border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:15px;">
            <h2>Tytuł karty</h2>
            <p>To jest przykładowy opis frontu.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back face -->
        <div class="back">
            <h2>Backside Title</h2>
            <p>Treść z tyłu karty – możesz tu umieścić dodatkowe informacje lub przyciski.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` | Creates a 3D space so the rotation looks realistic. |
| **2** | `.card` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Allows its child elements (`.front`, `.back`) to maintain their 3D positions. |
| **3** | On hover, `.card` gets `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | Rotates the whole card 180° around the vertical axis. |
| **4** | Both faces have `backface-visibility:hidden` | Hides the backside when it’s facing away from the viewer. |
| **5** | `.back` starts with `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | Keeps it hidden until the parent rotates. |

#### Customization tips

- Change `rotateY` to `rotateX` if you prefer a vertical flip instead of horizontal.
- Adjust the `transition` duration or timing function for faster/slower animation.
- Add more layers or use `box-shadow` to give depth.
- Replace the placeholder image URL with your own picture or icon.

Happy coding!
